// TEMPLATE — copy this file to `Mapbox.local.xcconfig` in this same directory and paste your token
// in below. The copy is gitignored; this template is committed.
//
//     cp App/Config/Mapbox.local.xcconfig.example App/Config/Mapbox.local.xcconfig
//
// Then edit `App/Config/Mapbox.local.xcconfig` and put your token after the `=`. Nothing else needs
// to change: `App/Config/Mapbox.xcconfig` already ends with
//
//     #include? "Mapbox.local.xcconfig"
//
// which is the optional include, so the file is picked up as soon as it exists and its absence is
// not a build error.
//
// ## Which token
//
// The PUBLIC (`pk.…`) token — the one Mapbox shows on your account's Tokens page as the default
// public token. It ships inside every built app and is designed to be embedded; it is untracked here
// at the owner's request, not because it is dangerous.
//
// Do NOT put the SECRET (`sk.…`) token here. That one is scoped `Downloads:Read` and is a build-time
// credential for SwiftPM's package resolution — it belongs in `~/.netrc` only, with `chmod 0600`,
// and never in this repository, in `Info.plist`, or in the app. `MapboxSetup.configure()` refuses
// anything that does not begin `pk.`, so pasting it here fails loudly rather than shipping it.
//
// ## The line to edit
//
// Uncomment and fill in — the `=` with nothing after it is what the committed base file already
// sets, so leaving this file empty is the same as not having it at all:

# MBX_ACCESS_TOKEN = pk.your_public_token_here
